title: Dashboard › Filters › Clear filters and empty states
route: /dashboard?payer=cardinal&program=iop&type=recertification&stage=appeal
intro: When 'Clear filters' appears, what it resets, and what the page shows when the filters match nothing.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Pick Payer, Program, Request type or Stage\nAny one that is not 'All'"
decision d1 "Is at least one of the four menus not 'All'?\nA grouping such as Needs you counts"
screen sc1 "Filter bar\nGhost button 'Clear filters' appears after the four menus"
screen sc0 "Filter bar\nNo 'Clear filters' button\nAll four menus show 'All'"
click c1 "Click 'Clear filters' on the filter bar"
process p1 "Payer, Program, Request type and Stage (or the grouping) go back to 'All'"
store w1 "Filters"
process p2 "Address loses payer, program, type and stage"
process p3 "Table goes back to its first 8 rows"
screen sc2 "Dashboard shows every request again\n'Showing 8 of 40'"
end e1 "Back to the full list"
end e0 "Nothing to clear\nThe button appears as soon as a menu is not 'All'"

decision d2 "Do any requests match the filters?"
process p4 "Example: Cardinal, IOP, Recertification, Appeal or call"
screen em1 "Headline\n'No requests match these filters.'\n'The filters hide everything. Clear them to see every request again.'"
screen em2 "Key figures\nStill count every stage that the Payer, Program and Request type filters leave: '0' with 'nothing is waiting on you' or 'nothing due in the next day'\nThe Stage menu shows the count of each stage beside its name"
screen em3 "Requests card\n'Showing 0 of 0'"
overlay em4 "Empty state in the card\n'No requests match'\n'The filters hide everything. Clear them to see every request again.'"
decision d3 "Is a narrowing filter set?"
click c2 "Click 'Clear filters' in the empty state"
endx x1 "No 'Clear filters' button\nOnly possible if there were no requests at all"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Payer, Program, Request type and Stage"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| sc1 --> c1 --> p1 --> w1 --> p2 --> p3 --> sc2 --> e1
d1 -->|No| sc0 --> e0
w1 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| sc2
d2 -->|No| p4
p4 --> em1 & em2 & em3 & em4
em4 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| c2 --> p1
d3 -->|No| x1
sc1 -.-> g1
